From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nptl: build NPTL for the C33 without an MMU

NPTL needs an MMU except on ARM and Xtensa, whose no-MMU kernels give it
what it uses; the C33's does too.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>

--- a/extra/Configs/Config.in
+++ b/extra/Configs/Config.in
@@ -631,7 +631,7 @@
 		   !TARGET_h8300 && \
 		   !TARGET_hppa && \
 		   !TARGET_ia64 && \
-		   (ARCH_USE_MMU || TARGET_arm || TARGET_xtensa)
+		   (ARCH_USE_MMU || TARGET_arm || TARGET_xtensa || TARGET_c33)
 	help
 	  If you want to compile uClibc with NPTL support, then answer Y.
 
